.TH QUADRF-NTSC 1 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-ntsc \- decode and play an analogue video signal
.br
quadrf-ntsc-demod \- NTSC demodulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-ntsc
.br
.B quadrf-ntsc-demod
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadrf-ntsc
is the Camera Decoder launcher. It tunes the front-end with
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
runs the demodulator and pipes the result into mpv. The video output is chosen
from the environment: inside a graphical session mpv draws there, and only on a
bare console with a monitor attached does it go straight to KMS.
.PP
.B quadrf-ntsc-demod
reads IQ from the SoapySDR device, demodulates NTSC and writes raw yuyv422
frames at 640x480 on standard output. It is usually driven by
.BR quadrf-ntsc ,
but the raw stream can equally be redirected to a file or piped into ffmpeg.
.PP
The launcher starts on Raceband 5 (5806 MHz) and shows a short on-screen
reminder of the keys. The mpv window must have keyboard focus (click it).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Step Raceband channel R1–R8 and retune the RX LO. The channel name and
frequency flash on screen for about 1.5 s. Mouse wheel does the same.
.TP
.BR q ", " Escape
Quit mpv (stops the decoder).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/quadrf/ntsc_ch.lua
mpv script that maps Up/Down onto
.BR quadrf-jtag (1)
.IR freq= .
.SH BUGS
The decoder currently misbehaves when an HDMI display is attached to the Pi.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR mpv (1)
